==English==

===Etymology===
{{back-form|manipulation|lang=en}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/məˈnɪpjʊleɪt/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-manipulate.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|manipulat}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[move]], [[arrange]] or [[operate]] something using the [[hand]]s
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[influence]], [[manage]], [[direct]], [[control]] or [[tamper]] with something
# {{lb|en|transitive|medicine}} To [[handle]] and move a [[body]] part, either as an [[examination]] or for a [[therapeutic]] purpose
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[influence]] or [[control]] someone in order to achieve a specific purpose, especially one that is unknown to the one being manipulated and beneficial to the manipulator; to [[use]]

